.\" gzip-ng.1 -- gzip-ng manual page
.\" For conditions of distribution and use, see LICENSE.md
.TH GZIP\-NG 1 2026-10-12 gzip\-ng "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gzip\-ng \- compress or decompress gzip files in parallel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gzip\-ng
.RI [ option " ...]"
.RI [ file " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gzip\-ng
compresses each
.I file
into
.IR file .gz
and removes the original, as
.BR gzip (1)
does.
The deflate, inflate, and crc work is done by zlib\-ng.
With no
.IR file ,
or when
.I file
is
.BR \- ,
it filters standard input to standard output.
.PP
With
.B \-d
it turns
.IR file .gz
back into
.IR file .
A
.I file
named without the
.B .gz
suffix is read from
.IR file .gz .
.PP
An output file takes the mode and times of its input.
An output that already exists is left alone, with a warning, unless
.B \-f
is given.
.PP
Options and files may come in any order, and short options cluster.
A value follows its option as the next argument,
or directly after a short option, as in
.BR \-b64 .
The form
.BI \-\-option= value
is not accepted.
The argument
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.PP
Run under the name
.B gunzip
it presets
.BR \-d ,
and under
.B zcat
or
.B gzcat
it presets
.BR \-dc .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Operation
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-stdout ", " \-\-to\-stdout
Write to standard output and keep the input files.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompress ", " \-\-uncompress
Decompress.
Input that is not in gzip format is refused when the output is a file,
and passed through unchanged when the output is standard output.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test
Check the integrity of each file without writing anything.
With
.B \-v
each good file is reported.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List the compressed size, uncompressed size, ratio, and name of each file,
with a line of totals for more than one.
With
.B \-v
the method, crc, and time are listed too, and with
.B \-N
the name is the stored one.
The uncompressed size is the one the file records at its end,
which holds 32 bits of it.
Standard input cannot be listed.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep
Keep the input files.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite existing output files, and allow compressed data to go to a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-recursive
Descend into directories.
Compression skips the files that already end in
.BR .gz ,
and decompression and listing take only those.
Symbolic links found there are skipped.
Without this option a directory is skipped with a warning.
.TP
.B \-\-synchronous
Write each output to permanent storage before its input is removed.
.SS Compression
.TP
.BR \-1 " .. " \-9
Set the compression level, from fastest to smallest.
The default is
.BR \-7 .
.TP
.B \-\-fast
The same as
.BR \-1 .
.TP
.B \-\-best
The same as
.BR \-9 .
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-huffman
Use the Huffman only strategy, which does no string matching.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-rle
Use the run length strategy, which matches only runs of one byte.
.TP
.B \-\-filtered
Use the filtered strategy,
meant for the small values a filter or predictor produces.
.TP
.B \-\-fixed
Use the fixed codes strategy, which never builds Huffman codes of its own.
.TP
.B \-T
Copy the input to the output unchanged, without compressing it.
.TP
.B \-\-rsyncable
Make a plain stream friendly to
.BR rsync (1).
Output written in blocks always is.
.SS Blocks and threads
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-blocksize " \fIsize\fP"
Compress in independent blocks that average
.I size
KiB.
A suffix of
.B K
or
.B M
names the unit.
The largest block is 256M, and the default once blocks are in use is 128K.
The blocks are deflated on every CPU unless
.B \-p
says otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-processes " \fIn\fP"
Use
.I n
threads, where 0 picks the number of CPUs, up to 64.
When compressing, any value but 1 turns blocks on.
When decompressing, the default is 0, and 1 inflates serially.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-independent
Accepted for compatibility with
.BR pigz (1).
Blocks are always independent.
.SS Name and time
Compressing a file saves its name and modification time in the header.
Decompressing restores neither unless asked to.
Standard input has no name or time to save.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-name
Do not save or restore the name and time.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-name
Save and restore the name and time.
The decompressed file takes the stored name, in the directory of its input,
and the stored time.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-no\-time
Do not save or restore the time.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-time
Save and restore the time.
.SS Messages
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Report the name and the reduction of each file processed.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress warnings, and the reports of
.BR \-v .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version, and that of the zlib\-ng it was built with, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-license
Show the license and exit.
.SS Compatibility
.TP
.B \-A
Text mode, accepted for compatibility and without effect.
.SH PARALLEL OPERATION
Without
.B \-b
or
.BR \-p ,
compression writes one plain deflate stream on one thread.
.PP
With either, the input is cut into blocks,
and each block is deflated on its own, so no block depends on another.
The blocks are written in order as one ordinary gzip member,
which any gzip can read.
A block ends where the content says to,
so a change to the input moves the boundaries with it
and leaves the blocks past the change as they were.
.PP
Decompression uses every CPU by default.
Files written in blocks, by
.B gzip\-ng
or by
.BR "pigz \-i" ,
are inflated in parallel, and so are BGZF and MiGz files.
Any other gzip file is inflated serially.
The output is the same at every thread count.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every file was processed.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
A warning was given and no error occurred,
as when an output already exists or a directory is skipped.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compress
.I file
into
.IR file .gz
and remove the original.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gzip\-ng file
.EE
.RE
.PP
Compress on every CPU at the highest level, and keep the original.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gzip\-ng \-k \-9 \-p 0 file
.EE
.RE
.PP
Compress an archive from a pipe in blocks of 1 MiB on 8 threads.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
tar \-cf \- dir | gzip\-ng \-b 1M \-p 8 > dir.tar.gz
.EE
.RE
.PP
Decompress to standard output and keep the file.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gzip\-ng \-dc file.gz
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check every gzip file under a directory.
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
gzip\-ng \-rtv dir
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
The
.B GZIP
environment variable is not read.
.PP
Only the
.B .gz
suffix is known, and there is no option to name another.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gzip (1),
.BR pigz (1),
.BR rsync (1)
.PP
RFC 1952, the gzip file format.
